#use(std/xref)
#use(std/table)
#use(std/code)
#use(std/math: asciimath)

#section{YAMD Kitchen Sink}::

This document exercises every plugin at once. See the #ref("ir") and the
#ref("twopass") sections below — both referenced #emph{before} they are defined.

#toc

#section{Architecture}::

The compiler builds an #def("ir"){element IR}{a tree of tagged nodes the
backends serialize} rather than emitting HTML strings directly.

#section{Two-pass evaluation}::

We use #def("twopass"){two-pass evaluation}{collect then resolve} so that
#ref("ir") cross-references resolve regardless of order.

#section{Data}::

A table with a header row and #emph{markup} in a cell:

#table(header: 1)
	#row
		#cell: Name
		#cell: Role
	#row{#emph{Kiril}}{infra}

#section{Code}::

Raw code keeps its braces and hashes:

#code(lang: "python")
	def area(r): # circle
		return {"a": 3.14 * r ** 2}

Inline #code{x = 1} stays verbatim too.

#section{Math}::

The quadratic roots are #m{x = (-b +- sqrt(b^2 - 4a c)) / (2a)}, block form:

#math
	sum_(i=0)^n i^2 = n(n+1)(2n+1) / 6

#glossary
